cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these data, please cite both the paper and this archive."
title: "INFLUX aircraft mass balance analysis: code and per-transect results"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB and Python scripts and per-transect results for the aircraft mass balance analysis of methane
  emissions from Indianapolis (Marion County, Indiana) with 37 flights of the Indianapolis Flux Experiment
  (INFLUX), 2011 to 2016. The scripts compute the emission rates with four definitions of the background
  (Downwind Edge, Upwind, Adjusted ABL Upwind, Upwind Edge) and the emission rates of the South Side Landfill,
  run the sensitivity analyses of the Supporting Information, and draw the figures of the paper.
  The data folder holds Table S1 and Data Sets S1 to S4 of the paper. The README describes the
  inputs each script needs and the order in which to run them.
version: "1.0"
